1
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:04,040
What is time?

2
00:00:04,040 --> 00:00:06,160
We feel it everywhere.

3
00:00:06,740 --> 00:00:07,810
In the beat of a heart.

4
00:00:08,420 --> 00:00:10,240
In the light that fades at evening.

5
00:00:10,900 --> 00:00:12,360
In the quiet space between

6
00:00:12,440 --> 00:00:13,980
one thought and the next.

7
00:00:15,770 --> 00:00:17,460
And yet, the moment we try

8
00:00:17,540 --> 00:00:19,570
to hold it, it slips away.

9
00:00:22,980 --> 00:00:25,090
We seem to travel along a single road.

10
00:00:25,780 --> 00:00:28,380
Behind us lies the past: fixed,

11
00:00:28,720 --> 00:00:30,520
remembered, out of reach.

12
00:00:31,280 --> 00:00:33,710
Ahead lies the future: open,

13
00:00:34,070 --> 00:00:36,130
unformed, not yet written.

14
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:39,680
And between them, a thin

15
00:00:39,760 --> 00:00:41,960
bright edge we call now.

16
00:00:45,280 --> 00:00:47,260
But physics tells a stranger story.

17
00:00:49,160 --> 00:00:51,500
In Einstein's relativity, time is

18
00:00:51,540 --> 00:00:53,340
woven together with space into a

19
00:00:53,500 --> 00:00:55,720
single fabric, called spacetime.

20
00:00:56,600 --> 00:00:58,430
A moment is not only a when.

21
00:00:58,930 --> 00:01:01,290
It is a place, in four dimensions.

22
00:01:04,330 --> 00:01:05,840
And this fabric bends.

23
00:01:07,600 --> 00:01:09,800
Move fast enough, and your clock ticks

24
00:01:09,880 --> 00:01:11,740
slower than the clocks you left behind.

25
00:01:12,390 --> 00:01:13,910
Sink deeper into gravity,

26
00:01:14,260 --> 00:01:16,040
and time itself runs slow.

27
00:01:18,090 --> 00:01:19,320
This is not an illusion.

28
00:01:19,920 --> 00:01:21,620
Satellites above us must correct

29
00:01:21,700 --> 00:01:24,230
their clocks for it, every single day.

30
00:01:26,240 --> 00:01:27,980
So there is no single now,

31
00:01:28,200 --> 00:01:29,840
shared by the whole universe.

32
00:01:30,530 --> 00:01:32,400
Each of us carries our own time.

33
00:01:35,760 --> 00:01:37,440
Some physicists go further.

34
00:01:38,150 --> 00:01:40,640
If past, present and future are all

35
00:01:40,720 --> 00:01:42,620
part of one four-dimensional block,

36
00:01:43,120 --> 00:01:45,210
then perhaps nothing truly passes.

37
00:01:47,070 --> 00:01:49,410
Every moment simply is, laid

38
00:01:49,500 --> 00:01:51,130
out like the frames of a film.

39
00:01:54,370 --> 00:01:55,980
And yet, we remember the

40
00:01:56,220 --> 00:01:57,930
past, never the future.

41
00:01:58,850 --> 00:02:00,440
Order gives way to disorder.

42
00:02:01,060 --> 00:02:02,090
Coffee cools.

43
00:02:02,480 --> 00:02:03,660
Stars burn out.

44
00:02:04,220 --> 00:02:06,260
And the arrow points only one way.

45
00:02:09,670 --> 00:02:11,380
So does time truly flow?

46
00:02:12,120 --> 00:02:13,340
Or is the flow something we

47
00:02:13,460 --> 00:02:15,660
bring to it: a story the mind

48
00:02:15,700 --> 00:02:17,840
tells, one moment at a time?

49
00:02:20,020 --> 00:02:21,400
Perhaps the deepest question

50
00:02:21,480 --> 00:02:22,800
is not what time is.

51
00:02:24,500 --> 00:02:26,820
But why it feels like anything at all.
